# cut-v0b — animatic re-timed to the revised script

Built from director `direction/script.md` + `direction/shot-list.md` at fb1a5b49dd17fb83ae53f01048bb1f6d14d3d4ce
(233 spoken words, shot 13 split into 13a/13b) with `tools/timeline.py` and rendered with `tools/conform.py`.
Picture: one slate per shot; end title final. Sound: none yet; scratch subtitles stand in for the read.

**Timing method.** Line lengths are estimated at 2.4 words/s + 0.2 s (the script's pace) until the recorded takes land.
Each shot holds its lines 0.3 s after its head, 0.3 s apart, 0.3 s before its tail (+1 s after line 8 for the strike);
the shot list's extra length is scaled so the cut lands on 120.000 s. Speech is 101.7 s of it, so there is only ~4 s of
slack left over the minimum: a slower read than 2.4 words/s pushes the cut toward 125 s.

